# Multi-Tenancy

## ITenantContext

- Resolved in middleware from JWT `tenant_id` claim — never from request body.
- Inject `ITenantContext` in handlers; do not pass `TenantId` as command parameter from API.

## Entity Rules

- All tenant-scoped entities inherit `BaseEntity` with `TenantId`.
- Global query filter applied in `DbContext.OnModelCreating` — do not manually filter unless bypassing for super-admin.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — trusting client
public record CreateStudentCommand(Guid TenantId, string Name);

// ✅ GOOD — tenant from context
entity.TenantId = _tenantContext.TenantId;
```

## Super-Admin Exception

- Super-admin endpoints (tenant provisioning) use explicit `[SuperAdminOnly]` policy.
- Must NOT use tenant query filter bypass unless audited and justified.

## Cache Keys

- Prefix all Redis keys: `tenant:{tenantId}:{key}`

## Tests Required

- Every new entity: add `TenantIsolationIntegrationTest` proving cross-tenant read/write fails.
